The docs-render port provides an Inja-powered host CLI tool and CMake helper
to render documentation with live code snippets, optional JSON metadata, and
verified executable outputs.

Add as a host dependency in vcpkg.json:

    "dependencies": [
      {
        "name": "docs-render",
        "host": true
      }
    ]

In-place mode (no .in file needed; updates <!-- inja: ... --> blocks in place):

    find_package(docs-render CONFIG REQUIRED)

    docs_render_add_targets(
        IN_PLACE README.md
        TARGETS my-example
    )

Template mode (renders OUTPUT from TEMPLATE; DATA is optional and only needed
when referencing JSON metadata such as {{ vcpkg.version }}):

    find_package(docs-render CONFIG REQUIRED)

    docs_render_add_targets(
        TEMPLATE README.md.in
        OUTPUT README.md
        DATA vcpkg=vcpkg.json
        TARGETS my-example
        TIMEOUT 15
    )

Available custom targets:
    docs-render       - Render documentation (skips write if unchanged)
    docs-render-check - Fail with exit code 1 if documentation is out of date

Optional vcpkg feature:
    Enable "features": ["skills"] in vcpkg.json to install the AI agent skill
    into share/agent-skills/docs-render.
